# Test: IS-IS flooding SNP wire format (spec-isis-7 flooding / CSNP / PSNP).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-isis-7-flooding -- the Complete and Partial Sequence Numbers
#            PDUs this spec builds for LSDB synchronization decode end-to-end
#            through the user-facing `ze isis decode` CLI: an L2 CSNP carrying the
#            whole LSP-ID range and a TLV 9 (LSP Entries) record, and an L2 PSNP
#            carrying a TLV 9 ack/request record (User Stories 1, 2, 4). The TLV 9
#            entry (Remaining Lifetime, LSP ID, Sequence Number, Checksum) is the
#            unit CSNP/PSNP exchange to detect gaps and acknowledge LSPs.
# PREVENTS:  a regression in the CSNP/PSNP body codec or the TLV 9 entry layout
#            isis-7 builds (start/end LSP-ID range, the 16-octet entry) reaching
#            the offline decode path.
#
# The fixtures below are PINNED to the codec by
# internal/plugins/isis/packet/flood_ci_test.go (TestISISFloodCIFixtures): if a
# codec/encoder change alters the bytes, that Go test fails alongside this .ci, so
# the functional fixture and the build path cannot drift.
#
# Live reliable flooding (a three-node line A->B->C converging its LSDB, the
# periodic SRM-driven flood timer, CSNP/PSNP request/ack, the P2P initial CSNP at
# adjacency Up, and purge re-flood + age-out) needs raw L2 (AF_PACKET) on a Linux
# veth and is proven by:
#   - the in-memory engine wiring tests (run on any host, including darwin):
#     TestISISLSDBSync (three-node line), TestISISFloodSRMTimer,
#     TestISISCSNPGapRequest, TestISISPSNPAck (internal/plugins/isis), and the
#     lsdb-package unit tests (TestFreshnessCompareMatrix, TestSRMDrivenSend,
#     TestCSNPGapRequestPending, TestPSNPRequestAndAck, ...); and
#   - the QEMU integration tests + the FRR interop scenarios isis-p2p-frr /
#     isis-lan-dis-frr owned by spec-isis-13.
# This functional test exercises the SNP wire format only: hex PDU -> ze
# isis decode -> JSON.

# --- L2 CSNP: whole-range digest with one TLV 9 LSP-entry. -------------------
# Source 0000.0000.0002.00, range [0000.0000.0000.00-00 .. ffff.ffff.ffff.ff-ff],
# TLV 9 entry for LSP 0000.0000.0001.00-00 seq 7 lifetime 1000 checksum 0x1234.
stdin=isis-csnp:hex=83210106190100000033000000000002000000000000000000ffffffffffffffff091003e80000000000010000000000071234
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze isis decode:stdin=isis-csnp:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="type":"l2-csnp"
expect=stdout:contains="source-id":"0000.0000.0002.00"
expect=stdout:contains="start-lsp-id":"0000.0000.0000.00-00"
expect=stdout:contains="end-lsp-id":"ffff.ffff.ffff.ff-ff"
expect=stdout:contains="type":9
expect=stdout:contains="value":"03e80000000000010000000000071234"

# --- L2 PSNP: a TLV 9 ack/request record. -----------------------------------
# Source 0000.0000.0002.00, TLV 9 entry for LSP 0000.0000.0001.00-00 seq 7.
stdin=isis-psnp:hex=831101061b010000002300000000000200091003e80000000000010000000000071234
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze isis decode:stdin=isis-psnp:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="type":"l2-psnp"
expect=stdout:contains="source-id":"0000.0000.0002.00"
expect=stdout:contains="type":9
expect=stdout:contains="value":"03e80000000000010000000000071234"
